---
// Installation & usage guide. Two personas: (1) use a taste to build UI,
// (2) create & share your own taste. Skills install via `npx skills add`
// (vercel-labs/skills — scans this repo's /skills directory).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Getting started — DESIGN.roblox.md">
  <div class="wrap guide">
    <header class="guide-head">
      <h1>Getting started</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        DESIGN.roblox.md is a plain-text design system your AI agent reads to
        build coherent Roblox UI — no design knowledge required. Install a
        <strong>skill</strong> once, pick a <strong>taste</strong> from the
        catalog, and prompt.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="path" aria-labelledby="path1">
      <h2 id="path1">Build UI with a catalog taste</h2>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Install the skill</h3>
          <p>One command, from your project root:</p>
          <pre><code>npx skills add ohzw/roblox-design-md --skill designmd-to-react-lua</code></pre>
          <p class="aside-line">
            Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and any
            <a href="https://skills.sh">Agent Skills</a>-compatible agent.
            Prefer manual? Copy <code>skills/designmd-to-react-lua/</code> from
            the repo into your project's skills directory — the skill is
            self-contained.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Add react-lua to your Roblox project</h3>
          <pre><code># wally.toml
[dependencies]
React = "roblox/react@17.3.9"
ReactRoblox = "roblox/react-roblox@17.3.9"</code></pre>
          <p>
            then <code>wally install</code>. Rojo or Argon project assumed —
            the skill knows the rest, including the jsdotlua scope if you
            prefer it.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Pick a taste</h3>
          <p>
            Browse the <a href="/#catalog">catalog</a>, open a taste, hit
            <strong>Copy DESIGN.roblox.md</strong> (or Download), and put the
            file in your project root.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Prompt your agent</h3>
          <pre><code>Using DESIGN.roblox.md, build the HUD: left side-button column,
top-right currency pills, bottom-center primary action. react-lua.</code></pre>
          <p>
            The skill enforces the load-bearing conventions for you:
            Scale-first layout, UIListLayout delegation, safe areas, ZIndex
            rules, exact react-lua syntax, motion tokens.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          <strong>Optional but recommended:</strong> Roblox Studio's built-in
          MCP server lets the agent verify its own work (play → screenshot →
          fix). The skill uses it automatically when connected, and UI-Labs
          stories are generated for every component so you can eyeball
          everything in Studio.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="path" aria-labelledby="path2">
      <h2 id="path2">Create &amp; share your own taste</h2>
      <p class="path-lede">
        The catalog is meant to be community-built: extract a taste from
        screenshots, verify it, share it.
      </p>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Install the extraction skill</h3>
          <pre><code>npx skills add ohzw/roblox-design-md --skill screenshot-to-designmd</code></pre>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Feed it screenshots</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Required:</strong> HUD full view · a window (shop, settings…) · a screen with 2+ buttons</li>
            <li><strong>Recommended:</strong> inventory grid, popup with dim, reward moment, progress bar</li>
            <li><strong>Optional:</strong> a 3–10s video of open/close/press for motion</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The skill tells you exactly what's missing and marks gaps honestly
            (<code>confidence: low</code>) instead of inventing values.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Validate</h3>
          <pre><code># in the catalog repo:
node tools/linter/lint.mjs DESIGN.roblox.md   # 0 errors required</code></pre>
          <p class="aside-line">
            Installed the skill standalone? It carries the full spec
            (<code>references/spec/</code>) and validates against it — an npm
            CLI (<code>npx designmd-roblox-lint</code>) is planned.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h3>Share</h3>
          <p>
            Entries need a real-device preview — screenshots of the generated
            UI running in Studio — before they're published; the catalog marks
            entries without one as <em>preview pending</em>. Submission flow
            (PR / request form) opens with the public launch.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="rules" aria-labelledby="rules-h">
      <h2 id="rules-h">Rules of the road</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Tastes describe publicly observable style conventions — colors,
          shapes, motion habits. Never copy assets, logos, or names from other
          games.
        </li>
        <li>Name entries by taste (<code>cartoon-chunky</code>), not by game.</li>
        <li>
          Your own game's design system is yours — share it under its real
          name if you like.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { padding-top: var(--space-2xl); max-width: 880px; }

  .guide-head h1 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .sub {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .sub strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .path { margin-top: var(--space-section); }
  .path h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .path-lede { color: var(--muted); margin-top: var(--space-sm); max-width: 56ch; }

  /* numbered steps — a real sequence, so the numbers carry meaning */
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .steps > li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 4rem;
  }
  .steps > li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -0.25rem;
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--crimson);
    color: var(--on-crimson);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }
  /* connector between steps */
  .steps > li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.1875rem;
    top: 2.75rem;
    bottom: calc(-1 * var(--space-xl) + 0.5rem);
    width: 2px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
  }
  .steps h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .steps p, .steps li li { font-size: var(--text-base); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 62ch; }
  .steps ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: var(--space-xs) 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-2xs); }
  .steps ul li::marker { color: var(--crimson); }

  pre {
    background: var(--code-bg);
    color: var(--code-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0;
  }
  /* direct children only — a bare `li code` would also hit `pre > code`
     inside the numbered steps and wash the dark blocks out */
  p > code, li > code, .aside-line > code {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    font-size: 0.8125em;
  }

  .aside-line { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .soon {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.5625rem;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    background: var(--crimson-wash);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }
  .note p { font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 68ch; }

  .rules { margin-top: var(--space-section); }
  .rules h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .rules ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); max-width: 68ch; }
  .rules li { line-height: 1.65; }
  .rules li::marker { color: var(--crimson); }
</style>
